Chapter: BritainShopHours
  cites Uoaix chapter TownLive
  cites Uoaix chapter ShopStock
  cites Uoaix chapter MageryState
  cites Uoaix chapter GameCombatPackets
  cites Uoaix chapter KeeperLeisure

 Shops trade from game hour 8 to 20 (root, 2026-10-07). The innkeeper (shop 5) lives at the inn, whose doors are the
 shared lodging's and never bar. A door within 4 tiles of a shop's reference region is that shop's.
  bsh-open-hour : Integer = 8
  bsh-close-hour : Integer = 20
  bsh-inn : Integer = 5
  bsh-reach : Integer = 4
  BshKeeper = record { home : BbSpot, work : BbSpot, tavern : BbSpot, concert : BbSpot, walk : RteWalk, next-step : Integer, goal : Integer, via-home : Integer, settled : Integer }
 A keeper spends two hours at the Blue Boar after closing, then goes home (one role, val S2, BritainShops.md).
  bsh-tavern-hour : Integer = 22
  bsh-goal : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  bsh-goal (i) (seconds) = let hour = int-mod (seconds / 3600) 24
    in if bsh-never-closes i then 1
    else if i == bb-musician then (if bsh-shop-open i seconds then 1 else 0)
    else if bsh-open seconds then 1 else if hour >= bsh-close-hour & hour < bsh-tavern-hour then 2 else 0
 Healers and taverns never close (Damian, 2026-10-10): the healer, the innkeeper and the tavern keeper trade at every hour,
 in every city (ct-shop-roles). The Conservatory's musician plays from 18 to midnight (UOAIX-222).
  bsh-healer : Integer = 4
  bsh-never-closes : Integer -> Boolean
  bsh-never-closes (i) = i == bsh-healer | i == bsh-inn | i == bb-tavern-keeper
  bsh-concert-hour : Integer = 18
  bsh-shop-open : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  bsh-shop-open (i) (seconds) = if bsh-never-closes i then True
    else if i == bb-musician then int-mod (seconds / 3600) 24 >= bsh-concert-hour
    else bsh-open seconds
 A musician at its post plays a well-played lute (0x4C in the 1.25 SOUNDIDX.MUL) once a game minute, heard through the
 event ring by every player in range (the town step's own packets are dropped by the timer drain).
  bsh-lute-sound : Integer = #4C
  bsh-play-seconds : Integer = 60
  bsh-plays : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  bsh-plays (i) (goal) = i == bb-musician & goal == 1
  BshStaff = record { keepers : List BshKeeper, door-rows : List Integer, door-shops : List Integer, door-nights : List Integer, phase : Integer, leisure : Integer }
  bsh-open : Integer -> Boolean
  bsh-open (seconds) = let hour = int-mod (seconds / 3600) 24 in hour >= bsh-open-hour & hour < bsh-close-hour
 A night runs from one closing to the next opening; its number changes at each opening hour.
  bsh-night : Integer -> Integer
  bsh-night (seconds) = (seconds + (24 - bsh-open-hour) * 3600) / 86400
  bsh-next-change : Integer -> Integer
  bsh-next-change (seconds) = let day = seconds / 86400 * 86400
    in let hour = int-mod (seconds / 3600) 24
    in if hour < bsh-open-hour then day + bsh-open-hour * 3600
    else if hour < bsh-close-hour then day + bsh-close-hour * 3600
    else if hour < bsh-tavern-hour then day + bsh-tavern-hour * 3600
    else day + 86400 + bsh-open-hour * 3600
 UOAIX-224 (Damian, 2026-10-09: "Tinker Shop closed, till 8am (35 minutes)"). The real wait is the game wait at the
 panel's day length, day-seconds real seconds a game day; 7200 is GameClock's default day, as in cg-game-ms.
  bsh-row-shop : BshStaff, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  bsh-row-shop (s) (row) (j) = if j == list-length s.door-rows then -1
    else if list-at s.door-rows j == row then list-at s.door-shops j else bsh-row-shop s row (j + 1)
  bsh-hour-text : Integer -> Text
  bsh-hour-text (h) = if h == 0 then "12am" else if h < 12 then show h & "am" else if h == 12 then "12pm" else show (h - 12) & "pm"
  bsh-count-text : Integer, Text -> Text
  bsh-count-text (n) (noun) = show n & " " & noun & (if n == 1 then "" else "s")
  bsh-wait-text : Integer -> Text
  bsh-wait-text (minutes) = if minutes < 60 then bsh-count-text minutes "minute"
    else if int-mod minutes 60 == 0 then bsh-count-text (minutes / 60) "hour"
    else bsh-count-text (minutes / 60) "hour" & " " & bsh-count-text (int-mod minutes 60) "minute"
  bsh-door-note : BshStaff, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  bsh-door-note (s) (row) (raw) (seconds) (day-seconds) = let shop = bsh-row-shop s row 0
    in if shop < 0 | bit-and raw 4 == 0 then "" else bsh-closed-note shop seconds day-seconds
 A closed shop's note for role shop ("" while open), said at its barred door and by its keeper (every city's shop speaks as
 its Britain role).
  bsh-closed-note : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  bsh-closed-note (shop) (seconds) (day-seconds) = if shop < 0 | shop >= bb-shop-count | bsh-shop-open shop seconds then ""
    else let hour = if shop == bb-musician then bsh-concert-hour else bsh-open-hour
    in let at = int-mod seconds 86400
    in let opens = hour * 3600
    in let wait = if at < opens then opens - at else 86400 - at + opens
    in let real = wait * (if day-seconds > 0 then day-seconds else 7200) / 86400
    in let minutes = if real < 60 then 1 else (real + 59) / 60
    in let entry = list-at bb-shops shop
    in (if shop == bb-musician then entry.premises else entry.title & " Shop") & " closed, till " & bsh-hour-text hour & " (" & bsh-wait-text minutes & ")"
  bsh-mask : Integer -> Integer
  bsh-mask (seconds) = bsh-mask-from seconds 0
  bsh-mask-from : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  bsh-mask-from (seconds) (i) = if i == bb-shop-count then 0
    else (if bsh-shop-open i seconds then 0 else bit-shl 1 i) + bsh-mask-from seconds (i + 1)
  bsh-inside : BbShop, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  bsh-inside (shop) (x) (y) (reach) = x >= shop.x1 - reach & x <= shop.x2 + reach & y >= shop.y1 - reach & y <= shop.y2 + reach
  bsh-keepers : Integer, List BshKeeper -> List BshKeeper
  bsh-keepers (i) (xs) = if i == bb-shop-count then xs
    else bsh-keepers (i + 1) (list-push xs (BshKeeper { home = BbSpot { x = 0, y = 0, z = 0 }, work = BbSpot { x = 0, y = 0, z = 0 },
      tavern = BbSpot { x = 0, y = 0, z = 0 }, concert = BbSpot { x = 0, y = 0, z = 0 }, walk = rte-walk 0, next-step = 0, goal = -1, via-home = 0, settled = 0 }))
  bsh-tavern-taken : List BshKeeper, BbSpot, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  bsh-tavern-taken (keepers) (spot) (count) (i) = if i == count then False
    else let h = (list-at keepers i).tavern
    in if h.x == spot.x & h.y == spot.y & h.z == spot.z then True else bsh-tavern-taken keepers spot count (i + 1)
  bsh-tavern : TownLive, WalkMap, List BshKeeper, Integer, Integer -> Result BbSpot Text
  bsh-tavern (t) (map) (keepers) (count) (offset) = when bb-placement t.vendors.game.world map tl-tavern-region offset
    is Err (e) -> Err e
    is Ok (spot) -> if not (tl-tavern-used t spot 0) & not (bsh-tavern-taken keepers spot count 0) then Ok spot
      else bsh-tavern t map keepers count ((spot.y - tl-tavern-region.y1) * (tl-tavern-region.x2 - tl-tavern-region.x1 + 1) + spot.x - tl-tavern-region.x1 + 1)
  bsh-taken : List BshKeeper, BbSpot, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  bsh-taken (keepers) (spot) (count) (i) = if i == count then False
    else let h = (list-at keepers i).home
    in if h.x == spot.x & h.y == spot.y & h.z == spot.z then True else bsh-taken keepers spot count (i + 1)
 A keeper's home is never a miner's, the gatherer's or the farmer's (reserved), so no two sleepers share a bed.
  bsh-reserved : List BbSpot, BbSpot, Integer -> Boolean
  bsh-reserved (reserved) (spot) (i) = if i == list-length reserved then False
    else let r = list-at reserved i
    in if r.x == spot.x & r.y == spot.y then True else bsh-reserved reserved spot (i + 1)
  bsh-home : TownLive, WalkMap, List BshKeeper, List BbSpot, Integer, Integer -> Result BbSpot Text
  bsh-home (t) (map) (keepers) (reserved) (count) (offset) = when bb-placement t.vendors.game.world map tl-home-region offset
    is Err (e) -> Err e
    is Ok (spot) -> if not (tl-spot-used t spot 0 0) & not (bsh-taken keepers spot count 0) & not (bsh-reserved reserved spot 0) then Ok spot
      else bsh-home t map keepers reserved count ((spot.y - tl-home-region.y1) * (tl-home-region.x2 - tl-home-region.x1 + 1) + spot.x - tl-home-region.x1 + 1)
  bsh-work : TownLive, WalkMap, WorldObject, BbShop -> Result BbSpot Text
  bsh-work (t) (map) (npc) (shop) = if bsh-inside shop npc.x npc.y 0 then Ok (BbSpot { x = npc.x, y = npc.y, z = npc.z })
    else bb-placement t.vendors.game.world map shop 0
 A keeper the lodging cannot hold keeps its shop as its home.
  bsh-fill : List BshKeeper, TownLive, WalkMap, List BbSpot, Integer -> Result Integer Text
  bsh-fill (keepers) (t) (map) (reserved) (i) = if i == bb-shop-count then Ok 0
    else let k = list-at keepers i
    in when world-get t.vendors.game.world (list-at t.vendors.vendors i).serial
      is Err (_) -> let idle = __record-set k "next-step" tl-max-seconds in bsh-fill keepers t map reserved (i + 1)
      is Ok (npc) -> when bsh-work t map npc (list-at bb-shops i)
        is Err (e) -> Err e
        is Ok (work) -> let w = tl-copy-spot k.work work
          in let home = if i == bsh-inn then work else (when bsh-home t map keepers reserved i 0 is Err (_) -> work is Ok (spot) -> spot)
          in let h = tl-copy-spot k.home home
          in let tavern = when bsh-tavern t map keepers i 0 is Err (_) -> home is Ok (spot) -> spot
          in let v = tl-copy-spot k.tavern tavern
          in let concert = when bsh-concert t map keepers i 0 is Err (_) -> tavern is Ok (spot) -> spot
          in let c = tl-copy-spot k.concert concert
          in bsh-fill keepers t map reserved (i + 1)
 The door walks take the shops as a list bound once (bsh-new): a list constant is built again at every mention, and
 naming bb-shops for each shop of each door row kept 27 MB at boot.
  bsh-shop-of : List BbShop, WdState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  bsh-shop-of (shops) (doors) (row) (shop) = if shop == bb-shop-count then -1
    else if shop /= bsh-inn & bsh-inside (list-at shops shop) (wd-field doors row 0) (wd-field doors row 1) bsh-reach then shop
    else bsh-shop-of shops doors row (shop + 1)
  bsh-door-rows : List BbShop, WdState, BbSpot, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  bsh-door-rows (shops) (doors) (entrance) (i) (out) = if i == doors.count then out
    else if wd-field doors i 7 /= 1 | (wd-field doors i 0 == entrance.x & wd-field doors i 1 == entrance.y) | bsh-shop-of shops doors i 0 < 0 then bsh-door-rows shops doors entrance (i + 1) out
    else bsh-door-rows shops doors entrance (i + 1) (list-push out i)
  bsh-door-shops : List BbShop, WdState, List Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  bsh-door-shops (shops) (doors) (rows) (i) (out) = if i == list-length rows then out
    else bsh-door-shops shops doors rows (i + 1) (list-push out (bsh-shop-of shops doors (list-at rows i) 0))
  bsh-nights : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  bsh-nights (n) (out) = if n == 0 then out else bsh-nights (n - 1) (list-push out (0 - 1))
  bsh-new : TownLive, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, List BbSpot, Integer -> Result BshStaff Text
  bsh-new (t) (map) (optional) (reserved) (leisure) =
    let keepers = bsh-keepers 0 (__list-with-capacity bb-shop-count)
    in let catalog = bb-shops
    in let rows = when optional is None -> [] is Just (doors) -> bsh-door-rows catalog doors t.entrance 0 []
    in let shops = when optional is None -> [] is Just (doors) -> bsh-door-shops catalog doors rows 0 []
    in if t.vendors.vendor-count < bb-shop-count then Err "Britain shop hours: keepers absent"
    else when bsh-fill keepers t map reserved 0
      is Err (e) -> Err e
      is Ok (_) -> Ok (BshStaff { keepers = keepers, door-rows = rows, door-shops = shops, door-nights = bsh-nights (list-length rows) [], phase = 0 - 1, leisure = leisure })
  bsh-away : TownLive, Integer -> Boolean
  bsh-away (t) (i) = when world-get t.vendors.game.world (list-at t.vendors.vendors i).serial
    is Err (_) -> True
    is Ok (npc) -> npc.health <= 0 | not (bsh-inside (list-at bb-shops i) npc.x npc.y bsh-reach)
 A closed shop's doors bar once each night, after its keeper has left; a picked bar stays open until the next night.
  bsh-bar : BshStaff, TownLive, WdState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  bsh-bar (s) (t) (doors) (now) (j) (changed) = if j == list-length s.door-rows then changed
    else let row = list-at s.door-rows j
    in let raw = peek-byte doors.opened row
    in let night = bsh-night now
    in let moved = if bsh-shop-open (list-at s.door-shops j) now then (if bit-and raw 4 == 0 then 0 else let cleared = wd-unbar doors row in 1)
      else if list-at s.door-nights j == night | raw /= 0 | not (bsh-away t (list-at s.door-shops j)) then 0
      else let noted = list-set-at s.door-nights j night in wd-bar doors row
    in bsh-bar s t doors now (j + 1) (changed + moved)
  bsh-at-work : BshStaff, Integer -> Boolean
  bsh-at-work (s) (i) = if i < 0 | i >= list-length s.keepers then True
    else let k = list-at s.keepers i in k.goal == 1 & k.settled == 1
  bsh-spot : BshKeeper, Integer -> BbSpot
  bsh-spot (k) (goal) = if goal == 0 then k.home else if goal == 2 then k.tavern else if goal == 3 then k.concert else k.work
 After closing a keeper goes where its leisure need sends it tonight (KeeperLeisure): the Blue Boar, the Conservatory or home.
  bsh-goal-of : BshStaff, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  bsh-goal-of (s) (i) (now) = let goal = bsh-goal i now in if goal == 2 then kl-choose s.leisure i (bsh-night now) else goal
 A keeper's concert tile is a free tile in the Conservatory's audience no other keeper holds.
  bsh-concert-taken : List BshKeeper, BbSpot, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  bsh-concert-taken (keepers) (spot) (count) (i) = if i == count then False
    else let h = (list-at keepers i).concert
    in if h.x == spot.x & h.y == spot.y & h.z == spot.z then True else bsh-concert-taken keepers spot count (i + 1)
  bsh-concert : TownLive, WalkMap, List BshKeeper, Integer, Integer -> Result BbSpot Text
  bsh-concert (t) (map) (keepers) (count) (offset) = when bb-placement t.vendors.game.world map kl-concert-region offset
    is Err (e) -> Err e
    is Ok (spot) -> if not (bsh-concert-taken keepers spot count 0) then Ok spot
      else bsh-concert t map keepers count ((spot.y - kl-concert-region.y1) * (kl-concert-region.x2 - kl-concert-region.x1 + 1) + spot.x - kl-concert-region.x1 + 1)
  bsh-keeper : BshStaff, TownLive, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, Integer, Integer -> Result (List (List Integer)) Text
  bsh-keeper (s) (t) (map) (doors) (now) (i) =
    let k = list-at s.keepers i
    in let goal = bsh-goal-of s i now
    in if k.next-step > now & k.goal == goal then Ok []
    else when world-get t.vendors.game.world (list-at t.vendors.vendors i).serial
      is Err (_) -> Ok []
      is Ok (npc) -> if npc.kind /= 1 | npc.health <= 0 then Ok []
        else let changed = if k.goal == goal then 0 else
          let via = __record-set k "via-home" (if k.goal >= 0 & (goal == 0 | k.goal == 0) & not (tl-at npc (bsh-spot k goal)) then 1 else 0)
          in let selected = __record-set k "goal" goal
          in let unsettled = __record-set k "settled" 0
          in rte-drop k.walk
        in let target = if k.via-home == 1 then t.entrance else bsh-spot k k.goal
        in if tl-at npc target | (k.via-home == 0 & k.goal == 0 & tl-in-lodging npc) then
          (if k.via-home == 1 then let arrived = __record-set k "via-home" 0 in let cleared = rte-drop k.walk in Ok []
          else if bsh-plays i k.goal then let rest = __record-set k "next-step" (now + bsh-play-seconds) in let arrived = __record-set k "settled" 1 in let cleared = rte-drop k.walk
            in let heard = t.items.notice npc.x npc.y 0 0 0 (cbp-sound bsh-lute-sound npc) in Ok []
          else let rest = __record-set k "next-step" (bsh-next-change now) in let arrived = __record-set k "settled" 1 in let cleared = rte-drop k.walk
            in let paid = if k.goal == 2 | k.goal == 3 then kl-pay t.vendors s.leisure i (bsh-night now) k.goal else 0 in Ok [])
        else let moves = k.walk.moves
        in when rte-toward-budget t.nav t.vendors.game.world (Just t.vendors.game) map doors rte-any k.walk npc target.x target.y target.z bsh-plan-budget
          is Err (e) -> Err e
          is Ok (packets) -> let next = __record-set k "next-step" (now + (if k.walk.moves == moves then tl-retry-seconds else tl-move-seconds)) in Ok packets
 UOAIX-216: at most bsh-plans keepers start a route plan in one step. A goal change at opening (8) or the Blue Boar's hour (12)
 dropped every keeper's route and all of them planned in the same 100 ms step, about 19 ms of wall time a plan, 0.35 to 0.47 s in
 all (trial 43336, TICK SLOW 13.14); the rest wait a step, so the town opens over about 1.3 s.
  bsh-plans : Integer = 2
 A keeper's plan expands at most 16384 cells, about a seventh of Britain's 432 x 272 map: a failed search costs that bound.
  bsh-plan-budget : Integer = 16384
  bsh-will-plan : BshKeeper, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  bsh-will-plan (k) (goal) (now) = not (k.next-step > now & k.goal == goal) & (k.walk.route < 0 | k.goal /= goal)
  bsh-keepers-step : BshStaff, TownLive, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, Integer, Integer, List (List Integer) -> Result (List (List Integer)) Text
  bsh-keepers-step (s) (t) (map) (doors) (now) (i) (packets) = bsh-keepers-budget s t map doors now i packets bsh-plans (\stage -> 0)
  bsh-keepers-budget : BshStaff, TownLive, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, Integer, Integer, List (List Integer), Integer, (Integer -> Integer) -> Result (List (List Integer)) Text
  bsh-keepers-budget (s) (t) (map) (doors) (now) (i) (packets) (left) (mark) = if i == bb-shop-count then Ok packets
    else let marked = mark (4 + i)
    in let plans = bsh-will-plan (list-at s.keepers i) (bsh-goal-of s i now) now
    in if plans & left <= 0 then bsh-keepers-budget s t map doors now (i + 1) packets left mark
    else when bsh-keeper s t map doors now i
      is Err (e) -> Err e
      is Ok (moved) -> bsh-keepers-budget s t map doors now (i + 1) (packets & moved) (if plans then left - 1 else left) mark
 ServUO Data/containers.cfg: the strong box 0x0E80 opens gump 0x4B and the crate 0x0E3C gump 0x44.
  bsh-gump : Integer -> Integer
  bsh-gump (art) = if art == ss-box-art then #004B else #0044
  bsh-lock-box : GvWorld, Magery, Integer, Integer, Boolean -> Integer
  bsh-lock-box (v) (magic) (i) (art) (locked) = let box = ss-box v i art
    in if box == 0 then 0
    else if gsi-register magic.items box 0 (bsh-gump art) False False /= 0 then 0
    else when mgs-container magic box
      is Err (_) -> 0
      is Ok (_) -> let meta = list-at magic.definitions (world-slot magic.items.world box)
        in let set = __record-set meta "locked" locked
        in mgs-touch magic
 The strong box stays locked; the crate locks at closing. Each opening and closing relocks a picked box.
  bsh-locks : GvWorld, Magery, Boolean, Integer -> Integer
  bsh-locks (v) (magic) (open) (i) = if i >= ss-shops v then 0
    else let box = bsh-lock-box v magic i ss-box-art True
    in let crate = bsh-lock-box v magic i ss-crate-art (not open)
    in bsh-locks v magic open (i + 1)
  bsh-turn : BshStaff, GvWorld, Maybe Magery, Integer -> Integer
  bsh-turn (s) (v) (magic) (now) = let phase = if bsh-open now then 0 else 1
    in if s.phase == phase then 0
    else let turned = __record-set s "phase" phase
    in let emptied = if phase == 1 then gv-window-all v 0 else 0
    in when magic is None -> 1 is Just (m) -> let locked = bsh-locks v m (phase == 0) 0 in 1
 A list constant is built again at every mention, so the roles are bound once a call: ct-vendor-role named ct-shop-roles
 (about 150 entries) for each vendor of each 100 ms town step (UOAIX-216).
  bsh-shut : GvWorld, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  bsh-shut (v) (seconds) (i) (count) = bsh-shut-in v ct-shop-roles seconds i count
  bsh-shut-in : GvWorld, List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  bsh-shut-in (v) (roles) (seconds) (i) (count) = if i >= v.vendor-count then count
    else let role = if i < bb-shop-count then i else if i - bb-shop-count < list-length roles then list-at roles (i - bb-shop-count) else -1
    in let set = gv-set-shut v i (if role < 0 then False else not (bsh-shop-open role seconds))
    in bsh-shut-in v roles seconds (i + 1) (count + set)
  bsh-advance : BshStaff, TownLive, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, Maybe Magery, Integer -> Result (List (List Integer)) Text
  bsh-advance (s) (t) (map) (doors) (magic) (now) = bsh-advance-marked s t map doors magic now (\stage -> 0)
 UOAIX-216: mark names each stage as it starts (0 closing flags, 1 open/close turn, 2 door bars, 3 keepers, 4 + i keeper i), so the wheel's
 accounting can time them (cg-town-move).
  bsh-advance-marked : BshStaff, TownLive, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, Maybe Magery, Integer, (Integer -> Integer) -> Result (List (List Integer)) Text
  bsh-advance-marked (s) (t) (map) (doors) (magic) (now) (mark) =
    let m0 = mark 0
    in let closed = __record-set t.vendors "closed" (bsh-shut t.vendors now 0 0)
    in let m1 = mark 1
    in let turned = bsh-turn s t.vendors magic now
    in let m2 = mark 2
    in let barred = when doors is None -> 0 is Just (state) -> bsh-bar s t state now 0 0
    in let touched = if barred == 0 then 0 else world-item-touch t.vendors.game.world
    in let m3 = mark 3
    in bsh-keepers-budget s t map doors now 0 [] bsh-plans mark
